Comment (cmd/reconciler.go:429):
**Logic flaw (found on the RC stack after the rebuild): a remembered rejection is never reported after a restart.** `ladder` correctly skips a fetched overlay that `rememberedRejected` matches, but `startup` then neither sets `rc.attempted` nor `rc.lastOutcome`, so the first (and, with `If-None-Match` → 304, every later) report says `applied-revision: <last good>`, `attempted-revision: null`, `status: applied`. The API derives `pending` and the UI shows the instance as pending forever instead of `rejected: unsafe-changes` (RC: kube-prod-worker-3, `allow_inline_policies: false`, rev 37 with inline policies → was `rejected`, now `pending` after restart). The cache already persists `RejectedRecord{Revision, Status, Reason, Error}`. Fix: in `startup` (and anywhere else `targetOverlay` falls back for the same reason), when `cache.Fetched` is remembered-rejected for this base, set `rc.attempted = &fetched.Revision` and `rc.lastOutcome = &applyError{Status: r.Status, Reason: r.Reason, Err: errors.New(r.Error)}` (Unsafe/PolicyErrors aren't persisted — either persist them in `RejectedRecord` (preferred, small) or accept their absence). Add a test: reject a revision, restart the reconciler on the same cache, assert the first report carries `attempted-revision` = that revision and `status`/`reason` = rejected/unsafe-changes.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** **lisa implementation guidance:** Fix: add rc.rememberedRejection(mode) in cmd/reconciler.go that, in apply modes, returns an applyError rebuilt from cache.Rejected (Status, Reason, Err from Error, Unsafe, PolicyErrors) when cache.Fetched is remembered-rejected for this base, and sets rc.attempted to the fetched revision. startup: use it as the outcome when the ladder produced none. reconcile: set attempted for a remembered-rejected fetched overlay even when the target falls back to applied, and after a successful prepare set rc.lastOutcome = rememberedRejection (not nil) so a re-prepare of the applied overlay (same-fingerprint file edit) does not clear the rejected status; the report call uses rc.lastOutcome. Persist Unsafe and PolicyErrors (capped) in agentstate.RejectedRecord as optional omitempty fields (old cache files keep their checksum). Test: reject rev N, start a new reconciler on the same state dir with the fetch returning 304, assert the first report has attempted-revision=N, status=rejected, reason=unsafe-changes and the persisted unsafe list.

